@startuml
title Curriculum drafts and remembered Admin editing
actor Administrator
participant "Admin browser" as Browser
participant "Admin gateway" as Gateway
participant "rbase Core" as Core
participant "GotIt Backend" as Product
database "Product database" as DB
participant "AI provider" as AI
Administrator -> Browser: Verify authenticator (once per 30 days)
Browser -> Gateway: OTP + current bearer login
Gateway -> Core: Verify TOTP
Core --> Gateway: Signed application/account/revision proof
Gateway --> Browser: HttpOnly SameSite cookie; lifetime only in JSON
Administrator -> Browser: Edit / request proposal / rehearse
Browser -> Gateway: Context + draft + stable operation UUID
Gateway -> Core: Check account, permissions and remembered proof
Gateway -> Product: Fixed authoring route + bearer + proof
Product -> Core: Independently authorize content.write
Product -> DB: Claim/replay scoped generation operation
alt Proposal or semantic review
  Product -> AI: Bounded structured content request
  AI --> Product: Candidate
  Product -> Product: Validate schema / scope / links
else Text or practice rehearsal
  Product -> Product: Shared planner/director or homework engine
  Product -> AI: Answer assessment when required
end
Product -> DB: Result receipt + audit metadata
Product --> Browser: Reviewable result (no learner evidence)
Administrator -> Browser: Accept selected changes
Browser -> Product: Save draft via authorized gateway
Product -> DB: Append draft snapshot
Administrator -> Browser: Explicitly publish
Browser -> Product: Publish with current revision and reason
Product -> Core: Recheck authorization
Product -> DB: Atomic content update + immutable snapshot + receipt
note over Product,DB
 Existing learner evidence and in-flight lesson snapshots remain historical.
 Reading acknowledgements bind an exact content hash and grant no mastery.
end note
@enduml
